<Pack>
	<!--
		TWO TIERS, AND THE FILENAME SAYS WHICH.

		`Tutorial C.L ` is the spine: ordered, CHAPTERED (decided 2026-09-24, see
		docs/CHAPTER-STRUCTURE-PROPOSAL.md). The chapter number names the question a unit answers;
		the lesson number orders the answers. Numbering is a CLAIM that order matters, so it is
		spent only here - and chapter.lesson makes the claim twice, locally: inserting a geometry
		lesson renumbers chapter 1 and nothing else.

		`Prompt ` is the library: unordered, unnumbered, skippable, no prerequisites. Numbering
		these would make the numbers noise and make a reader arriving in the middle feel late -
		when the entire point of the tier is that they are not.

		The Coding Train states the same split in its own words: Main Tracks "you can follow like
		a course syllabus", Side Tracks "don't necessarily need to be watched in order".

		The prefixes extend vvvv's existing Explanation / HowTo / Example convention, which is
		already three-quarters of Diataxis. `Tutorial` is the genre those three are missing.
		tools\Test-VLPackage.ps1 checks the prefix and the chapter.lesson contiguity, and checks
		this file against the disk in both directions.

		A THIN CHAPTER IS A LABELLED GROWTH SLOT, not a mistake: reprojection lands in chapter 3
		when it unblocks, raster/DEM in chapter 5, more network in chapter 6, the Act IV lab's
		output in chapter 7. QGIS's training manual ships one-lesson modules for the same reason.
	-->
